A||||2||Gerald||85 or 86? Which should I buy||||1||
Z||000000||Gerald||11-19-2001||01:03 AM||||Im looking into buying another Fiero. The duke is being a pain in the a$$ and im sick of my brothers Daytona being faster then my fiero. Im not a huge fan of the fastbacks so I think I want a areo notch back. What year/model was the best for a V6 notch back excluding the formula and 88 GT's?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brandon86SE||11-19-2001||01:24 AM||||I like my baby!  86SE, 2.8L, V6, 4spd, aero nose.  Basically you're looking at either an 85 GT, or an 86-88 SE.  Those are the only way for you to get the V6, notchback, aero nose combo.  Essentially they are the same car, except the 86 is a year newer.  With the 4 speed (85/86), I believe they are the fastest Fiero's made.  (lighter than GT's, 4spd gearing better 0-60, 1/4 than 5spd in Formula)  So really, it just comes down to what you find first!  Best of luck to ya!<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Brandon86SE (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||Kelvin Vivian||11-19-2001||02:27 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=0&courtesy=1">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=1&courtesy=1">  <BR>1987 SE I4 "The Duke"<P>Don't forget about 87, aero-notchbacks were available in this year too.  Although, not too many were produced:<P>1987 SE V6 = 2474<BR>1987 SE I4 = 1401<P>Some changes between the 1986 and 1987 Fiero models are: In 1987, all V6 Fieros had the getrag 5-spd, a larger gas tank (10.2g to 11.9g), and the headlight motors were upgraded.<P>KV<P>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 11-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||14
